Give autoloot a chance at Pickpocket's junk-box loot, not just chests.
Touches: src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp, Spell::EffectPickPocket()

Why: EffectPickPocket normally just calls player->SendLoot(target,
LOOT_PICKPOCKETING), which opens the manual loot window directly --
there was no hook here at all for a module to intervene, unlike the
GameObject chest path (GameObject::Use()'s OnPlayerUseGameObject). Since
Pickpocket doesn't kill its target, the existing creature-kill autoloot
hook (OnPlayerCreatureKill) never applies either -- junkboxes were the
one loot source autoloot could never reach.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp
@@ Spell::EffectPickPocket(SpellEffIndex effIndex)
+// Living Gear core-patch: pickpocket junkbox autoloot.
+bool LivingGear_TryAutolootPickpocket(Player* player, Unit* target);
+
 void Spell::EffectPickPocket(SpellEffIndex /*effIndex*/)
 {
     if (effectHandleMode != SPELL_EFFECT_HANDLE_HIT_TARGET)
         return;

     if (!m_caster->IsPlayer())
         return;

+    if (LivingGear_TryAutolootPickpocket(m_caster->ToPlayer(), unitTarget))
+        return;
+
     m_caster->ToPlayer()->SendLoot(unitTarget->GetGUID(), LOOT_PICKPOCKETING);
 }

LivingGear_TryAutolootPickpocket (LivingGear_Vault.cpp) replicates
Player::SendLoot's own LOOT_PICKPOCKETING fill logic (CanGeneratePickPocketLoot/
SetPickPocketLootTime/FillLoot/gold formula) exactly, since bypassing
SendLoot means that fill never happens otherwise, then grants the loot
the same deferred way chest autoloot does (Spell::EffectPickPocket is
still mid-execution on the caster when this runs -- same reentrancy
hazard as chest autoloot). Falls back to the normal SendLoot window
(returns false) if autoloot is off or the creature was already
pickpocketed, so the real "already pickpocketed" error message still
shows for that case.
